  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "text1528",
   "x": 1020,
   "y": 570,
   "width": 722.4000000000001,
   "height": 56.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#6e7781",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "seed": 1529,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1530,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "blue: 3% or worse, or nan on every window. pythia rows use the wikitext-2 windows from\nlm_quality.py (64 of 512), the rest 32 of 512. santacoder is scored on python code.\n* qwen: approximate edit on the slow dims, so the fp32 logits move.",
   "originalText": "blue: 3% or worse, or nan on every window. pythia rows use the wikitext-2 windows from\nlm_quality.py (64 of 512), the rest 32 of 512. santacoder is scored on python code.\n* qwen: approximate edit on the slow dims, so the fp32 logits move.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "text1531",
   "x": 1020,
   "y": 662,
   "width": 875.84,
   "height": 63.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1f2328",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "seed": 1532,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1533,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "santacoder overflows fp16 on every window and dropping the bias fixes it exactly. bloom-560m\nloses 13% in bf16 and dropping its bias of 183 changes nothing, so that loss comes from\nsomewhere else. a big invisible bias is not enough to predict damage.",
   "originalText": "santacoder overflows fp16 on every window and dropping the bias fixes it exactly. bloom-560m\nloses 13% in bf16 and dropping its bias of 183 changes nothing, so that loss comes from\nsomewhere else. a big invisible bias is not enough to predict damage.",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "text1534",
   "x": 1020,
   "y": 760,
   "width": 747.6,
   "height": 56.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#6e7781",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "seed": 1535,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1536,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "qwen2.5 has rotary on every dim, so nothing in it is exactly invariant. the hatched bars\non the left are its key bias in the dims that turn less than 0.1 rad over 4096 positions.\nzeroing that part moves the fp32 logits by 0.18 and perplexity by under 0.01%.",
   "originalText": "qwen2.5 has rotary on every dim, so nothing in it is exactly invariant. the hatched bars\non the left are its key bias in the dims that turn less than 0.1 rad over 4096 positions.\nzeroing that part moves the fp32 logits by 0.18 and perplexity by under 0.01%.",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
